Error [E-ERR-SIGIL]: `T ! E` and `T ? E` are retired infix fallible type spellings.
  --> tests/ui/retired_fallible_type_sigil.jet:3:12
    |
  3 | fn f() Int ! E -> Ok(1)
    |            ^
 Why: the success type and error type have one unambiguous prefix contract, so `?` keeps one meaning: possible absence when it prefixes a success type.
 Fix: write `?Entry !StoreError`, `Int !(DbError | TimeoutError)`, or `!IOError`; remove a bare `!` contract because failure is implicit.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-ERR-SIGIL

